## Anti-patterns — do NOT do these

Each line is a violation of the section in brackets.

1. A commit or rollback in the data-access layer, or more than one commit per mutation. [§2]
2. Trusting the tenant id or the author from the request body. [§4]
3. A list query with no tenant scope, or a wrong-tenant read that 403s instead of 404. [§4]
4. Float for money, or an amount with no currency. [§3]
5. Post-filtering search in the application, or an unescaped LIKE. [§8]
6. Sorting by a raw parameter with no allow-list. [§8]
7. Accepting a status or an assignment through the update schema. [§6]
8. Returning a parent after writing children on the same session. [§10]
9. An unguarded route, or a hardcoded role name. [§7]
9b. Feeding a dropdown from a gated list endpoint, or gating an options route. [§7]
10. A new database enum with no drop in the downgrade, or a model missing from the import file. [§12]
11. Heavy imports in `__init__.py`, or implicit lazy loading. [§3, §11]
12. Awaiting the audit call, or auditing inside the transaction. [§2]
13. A UTC date where a tenant calendar date belongs. [§16]
14. An inline HTTP error in a service or a route, including ownership and upload guards. [§11]
15. Interpolating a raw decimal quantity into text a person reads. [§16]
16. Re-resolving a counterparty by id at print time on an issued document. [§13]
17. Regenerating a stored document on download, or a cache key missing a live read. [§14]
18. Changing a cached list without clearing it after the commit. [§15]
19. Patching a module-level object by assignment in a test. It leaks into every later test. [tests]

## New-module checklist

Build in the §1 order, then: permissions in the catalogue → router in the aggregator → models in
the migration import file → a reversible migration → the module guide → tests, green →
a session handoff. Full walkthrough: `docs/CHECKLIST.md` Part 3.
